id: E7001-draft-2301_80739235
trigger_tool: cmake|clang|conan|runtests.pl|WSL
phase: configuration|compilation|target_validation|testing
error_signature: "fatal error: 'openssl/opensslv.h' file not found|postcheck FAILED|negative epoch|DrvFs|9p mount|BadZipFile: File is not a zip file|redefinition of 'sockaddr_storage'"
error_signature_ci: "uses_external_curl on name = \"curl\" despite tools.files.get|redefinition of 'sockaddr_storage' from linux/tcp.h and sys/socket.h"
severity: 2
category: cmake|dependency-closure|ohos|testing|windows
match_keywords: OpenSSL include root, CMake package layout, OHOS AArch64, DrvFs mtime, negative epoch, curl remote-time, WSL upstream test, codeload archive filename, linux/tcp.h, sockaddr_storage, CMake header probe
title: CMake dependency and platform header probes must match target layout and host filesystem boundaries
root_cause: The OHOS OpenSSL package exposed headers below a child openssl directory, so pointing OPENSSL_INCLUDE_DIR at that child made openssl/opensslv.h unreachable. Separately, WSL /mnt/f uses a DrvFs/9p filesystem that clamps negative Unix mtimes to epoch zero, making upstream tests that require pre-1970 timestamps fail independently of the product code. A codeload URL without a trusted archive suffix also allowed a worker to choose ZIP extraction for a gzip tar response, so tools.files.get() needed an explicit filename while retaining the original URL and hash. Finally, OHOS exposes linux/tcp.h beside sys/socket.h even though the two headers redefine sockaddr_storage, so the target must disable that optional header probe and use netinet/tcp.h.
affected_scope: CMake cross-builds consuming Conan packages with nested public headers or incompatible optional platform headers, and Windows-hosted WSL upstream suites that assert timestamps before 1970.
verification_cmd: "set OPENSSL_INCLUDE_DIR to the package root and HAVE_LINUX_TCP_H=OFF, rebuild; reproduce the filesystem boundary with Python os.utime on /mnt/f using a negative epoch"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: bind-package-root-separate-host-fs-boundary-explicit-archive-and-probe-format
rec_description: Bind CMake include and archive paths to the exact frozen package tree, explicitly name remote archive formats when URL suffixes are unreliable, disable only a target-proven incompatible optional header probe, then keep host filesystem limitations as explicit evidence rather than changing upstream assertions or claiming full test PASS.
rec_command: "-DOPENSSL_ROOT_DIR=<openssl-package> -DOPENSSL_INCLUDE_DIR=<openssl-package> -DOPENSSL_SSL_LIBRARY=<openssl-package>/lib/libssl.a -DOPENSSL_CRYPTO_LIBRARY=<openssl-package>/lib/libcrypto.a"
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-recipe-and-validation-contract
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: native-filesystem-validation
fallback_description: Run timestamp-sensitive upstream cases on a native filesystem that preserves negative mtimes, such as a task-private ext4 image stored under F: or the platform CI worker; never convert a DrvFs postcheck failure to PASS.
fallback_command: "platform CI: make -C build test-full"
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: platform-ci
forbid_1_pattern: "OPENSSL_INCLUDE_DIR=.*openssl$"
forbid_1_reason: The compiler then searches openssl/opensslv.h below a directory that is already the openssl include child.
forbid_1_consequence: Cross-build fails late after compiling most of the library.
forbid_2_pattern: "test_762.*PASS|ignore.*remote-time|disable.*mtime"
forbid_2_reason: A host filesystem limitation must not be hidden by weakening the upstream test or fabricating success.
forbid_2_consequence: The result no longer proves the upstream timestamp behavior.
forbid_3_pattern: "HAVE_LINUX_TCP_H=ON|include <linux/tcp.h> on OHOS"
forbid_3_reason: The OHOS sysroot's linux/tcp.h conflicts with sys/socket.h and redefines sockaddr_storage.
forbid_3_consequence: The target build fails in cf-socket.c or cf-ip-happy.c before producing the consumer library.
principles: P003, P007, P018
